\[
Q = \frac{\pi r^4 \Delta P}{8\mu L}
\]

where:
- \( Q \) is the fluid flow rate (volume per time)
- \( r \) is the radius of the tube
- \( \Delta P \) is the pressure difference between the two ends of the tube
- \( \mu \) is the viscosity of the fluid
- \( L \) is the length of the tube

The relationship is more complex in the blood document, but the general properties are consistent with this equation. 

