- Methanol and ethanol are both alcohols with relatively high vapor pressures, but methanol is more toxic (lower PEL).  
- MTBE has a very low PEL (100 ppm), suggesting it is highly toxic even at low concentrations, despite its moderate vapor pressure.  

In summary, while methanol and ethanol are volatile, their PELs reflect their toxicity differences. MTBE, despite having a lower vapor pressure than methanol, has the strictest PEL due to its high toxicity. Thus, vapor pressure alone does not determine PEL; toxicity is a critical factor.  

