\[ y(t) = e^{-\infty \int h(t) dt} \int g(t) e^{\infty \int h(t) dt} dt \]
The correct method to solve this equation is to use the integral function. The integral function \( \mu(t) \) is defined as:
\[ \mu(t) = e^{\infty \int h(t) dt} \]
Multiplying both sides of the equation by \( \mu(t) \):
\[ \mu(t) y' + \mu(t) h(t) y = \mu(t) g(t) \]
