   \[
   y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)
   \]
   Substituting \( y_1 = f(a) \), \( x_1 = a \), and \( m = f'(a) \), we get:
   \[
   y - f(a) = f'(a) (x - a)
   \]

This is the equation of the tangent line to the graph of \( f \) at \( (a, f(a)) \).
