Q = m_g * c_p * ΔT

1858.5 kJ = m_g * 1.005 kJ/kgK * 550 K

m_g = 1858.5 / (1.005 * 550)

m_g ≈ 3..35 kg

Now we can calculate the entropy change of the gases:

ΔS_gas = - (3.35 kg * 1.005 kJ/kgK * 550 K) / 825 K

ΔS_gas = - (1858.5 kJ) / 825 K

ΔS_gas ≈ -2.25 kJ/K

The total entropy change of the combined system is the sum of the entropy changes of the water and the gases:

ΔS_total = ΔS_water + ΔS_gas

ΔS_total ≈ 3.764 kJ/K + (-2.25 kJ/K)

ΔS_total ≈ 1.514 kJ/K

