The decay length \(l\) of the electromagnetic wave is given by:
\[
l = \frac{\lambda}{\frac{2\pi}{\text{Δn}}} = \frac{\lambda}{\frac{2\pi}{\Delta n}} = \frac{\lambda}{\text{k}}
\]
where:
- \( \lambda \) is the wavelength of the electromagnetic wave.
- \( \Delta n = n_{\text{cell}} - n_{\text{core}} \) is the difference in refractive indices.

